1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:02,980
Previously on JoJo's Bizarre Adventure!

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:06,757
I don't think I'm going to
be able to help you, folks.

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:10,899
It's been my job to repair rooftops
in Cairo for around 40 years now.

4
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:14,296
And I can't say that I've
ever seen a place like this.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,871
And my daughter's condition is much worse.

6
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:19,432
At best, she has three or four days left.

7
00:00:20,740 --> 00:00:22,400
I can almost feel it.

8
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,659
It's like Dio's right on top of us.

9
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:26,395
We should get moving.

10
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:29,286
We'll talk to everyone
here until we find him.

11
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,520
It's a real scorcher out here today.

12
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:42,020
I haven't had a shower in almost two days.

13
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,911
It's beginning to ruin my je ne sais quoi.

14
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:50,470
Huh?

15
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:54,120
Uh... Hmm.

16
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:01,770
Huh?

17
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:18,660
What's the big idea, asshole?

18
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:20,337
You got some kind of problem with me?

19
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:22,137
I've got a problem with
where you're sitting!

20
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:24,317
A cocky foreigner like you has no business

21
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,597
sitting here pretending
to be some kind of beggar!

22
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:27,997
Don't you have a lick of common sense?

23
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:30,400
Who said that you could sit here, huh?

24
00:01:30,740 --> 00:01:33,387
Ah, you must be a beggar
from a foreign land.

25
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,091
I know this isn't much But I hope it helps

26
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:39,040
Thanks, but

27
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:42,060
You back off pal.

28
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:43,161
This is my turf.

29
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:44,789
You poofy-haired blockhead

30
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:49,160
What's that supposed to hey hold a wrap?

31
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:54,660
Don't just sit there with your mouth agape
give that money to him immediately Hmm?

32
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:59,360
Oh, I get what's going
on here. He's a beggar.

33
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:01,877
You'll have to forgive my
friend's obliviousness.

34
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:04,497
He's not accustomed to
the rules of this city.

35
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:07,397
Why didn't you tell me you were
a beggar in the first place?

36
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:09,497
It's called having a shtick, you numbnut.

37
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:11,597
People around here know
me as a mute beggar.

38
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:14,757
There's something known as
a beggar's association here.

39
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,717
Beggars have their own
areas where they're paid

40
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,117
to do nothing but sit
around and beg all day.

41
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:20,937
While it may seem strange to us,

42
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:24,277
the rules they put in place help
keep everything running smoothly.

43
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:25,340
Get out.

44
00:02:25,980 --> 00:02:28,957
Yes, and that exchange from
earlier has hurt my pride.

45
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:33,277
I wonder if I'd make more money by
disguising myself as a foreign beggar.

46
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:36,597
The hobos, they are a changin'.

47
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:40,017
Oh, by the way, I thought I
recognized you from somewhere.

48
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:43,117
If I'm not mistaken, you're
Avdol the fortune teller.

49
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,440
Way I hear it, you got
spooked and fled to Japan.

50
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,277
Apparently, someone was
looking to kill you.

51
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:52,437
I'd rather discuss us needing
a favor from the one who knows

52
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:56,696
everything there is to know about
this area you'll be well compensated.

53
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:03,657
It's imperative that we find this
building as quickly as possible.

54
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,269
We're running out of time.

55
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:18,540
I've done enough work for one day.

56
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:24,844
You gents have my word that I'll
find the mansion in three hours.

57
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:25,920
Just sit tight.

58
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,720
By the way, did anyone
see where Iggy ran off to?

59
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:21,240
the end of the day,

60
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:23,397
when I'm in the end of the day,

61
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:27,460
I'm so good now!

62
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,400
When I'm in the end of the day,

63
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:39,817
I'm the one who's lost in my mind, I'm
going to continue to do this, the Crusaders!

64
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:42,620
That's her hand.

65
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:46,380
To the last page we do Give us your hand.

66
00:04:49,740 --> 00:04:51,120
End of the world.

67
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:54,845
That's my memory of the blood.

68
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:57,620
On the way!

69
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:58,690
On the way!

70
00:04:58,773 --> 00:05:00,920
On the way!

71
00:05:45,840 --> 00:05:48,660
Oh, my God.

72
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:10,890
Let's go.

73
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:04,640
that's the place all right mission
accomplished and it only took two hours

74
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:08,731
if it exists in this city you
can bet your ass i'll find it

75
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:10,730
Ugh!

76
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,212
Iggy thought to himself.

77
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:29,480
So, that bird is a stand user, same as me.

78
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:32,917
Given that it offed that guy
with a giant block of ice,

79
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,941
it must be the guard around here.

80
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:37,747
It'll kill anyone who
approaches the mansion.

81
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:43,520
Which means that bird's next
target is probably going to be me.

82
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:51,240
From early on,

83
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:53,897
the ancient Egyptians
recognized the prowess of

84
00:07:53,980 --> 00:07:57,037
the noble falcon soaring
high above the Nile Valley.

85
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:01,397
They trained the bird as a hunting partner
and considered it a symbol of Horus,

86
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:03,539
guardian deity of the royal family.

87
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:08,277
the falcon's vision is able to
spot prey from several kilometers

88
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:12,977
away its oculus is forever represented
by the eye of horus an emblem

89
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:17,997
of protection and royal power the
falcon soaring through the air is

90
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:22,900
called pet shop it is the wielder
of the stand horus god of the sky

91
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:27,417
nervously iggy thought
damn it this is just

92
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:30,460
my luck looks like i
stumbled on dio's mansion

93
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:34,657
Why'd I have to find this place
instead of one of the others?

94
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:39,034
What's worse, that falcon can use its
stand to shoot giant chunks of ice.

95
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,438
It's like a super-powered guard dog.

96
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:44,015
Actually, it's more like a guard bird.

97
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:55,300
Come on, you gotta be kidding me.

98
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:57,873
I couldn't care less about this Dio guy.

99
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,820
I got dragged here against my will,

100
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,417
like some head and forced to
be one of the Joestar's allies.

101
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,676
Like hell I'm gonna fight this thing.

102
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:11,252
All I want is a little Aranar, a girl
of my own, some place to settle down.

103
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:15,177
Fighting someone else's battle
isn't on my list of things to do.

104
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:18,817
Besides, even if I were to throw
down with Tweety over there,

105
00:09:18,900 --> 00:09:20,197
what would I get in return?

106
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,817
There's no way I'm putting
my life on the line.

107
00:09:22,900 --> 00:09:25,117
Time to bring out that
old dumb dog routine.

108
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:28,494
That bird brain will never
suspect them with those guys.

109
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,830
Those eyes.

110
00:09:56,913 --> 00:09:58,117
That's the thing about birds.

111
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:00,597
You can never tell what they're thinking.

112
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:02,520
I bet my stand could take him.

113
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:05,837
But then again, there's a reason I'm
making a fool out of myself here.

114
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:09,017
I've got nothing to do with
Jotaro and those other guys.

115
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:11,747
Go back to your mansion,
you feathered freak.

116
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,580
Huh? A bird?

117
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:22,977
What's with this bird?

118
00:10:23,060 --> 00:10:25,420
Why isn't the damn thing moving?

119
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:26,797
No, it's too late.

120
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:28,174
I'm gonna run it over.

121
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:41,917
I've never seen anything
like that bird in my life.

122
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,941
How could it fly under a
car so low to the ground?

123
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,989
It didn't even try to
dodge out of the way.

124
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:50,629
It dove without giving
it a second thought.

125
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:57,874
Crazy bastard, but it seems like the
freaks lost interest to me, for now.

126
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:00,410
Apparently,

127
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:04,697
it only goes on the offensive when people
try to make their way inside the mansion.

128
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:05,620
Even so,

129
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:08,937
if Jotaro and the others ever
end up finding this place,

130
00:11:09,020 --> 00:11:11,785
they'll have a hell of
a time trying to get in.

131
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:15,040
Oh well, that's their
problem to deal with.

132
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:19,220
Butch! Tiny! Butch! Tiny!

133
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,576
Where'd you guys go?

134
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:25,757
Hey, you haven't seen my
dogs around, have you?

135
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:28,397
Their names are Butch and
Tiny, if that helps at all.

136
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,600
Get the hell out of my face.

137
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,020
I'm a dog, pal.

138
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:34,657
Even if I knew, it's
not like I could answer.

139
00:11:34,740 --> 00:11:35,975
What are you, stupid?

140
00:11:39,580 --> 00:11:41,940
Oh no, that collar looks like...

141
00:11:42,780 --> 00:11:44,820
I was right, it's Tiny's.

142
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:47,926
I don't understand, why
is it under this gate?

143
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:49,857
And why is there blood on it?

144
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:51,440
Tiny and Butch?

145
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,659
Is he talking about those big dogs?

146
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:56,100
Tiny! Butch!

147
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:58,197
What's that kid thinking?

148
00:11:58,280 --> 00:12:01,617
If he tries going under the gate, he'll
have to face the wrath of that bird!

149
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,780
It'll murder him!

150
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:05,620
Tiny! Butch! Are you there?

151
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:08,500
Tiny! Butch!

152
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,320
Tiny! Butch!

153
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,217
I don't know why I'm getting so worked up.

154
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:19,535
If some human kid bites a
big one, It's not my problem.

155
00:12:20,180 --> 00:12:22,356
Survival of the fittest, as they say.

156
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:25,760
Stupid die first, as do
people who act recklessly.

157
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:29,137
I'd rather stay out of this, so...

158
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:30,060
Goodbye, kid.

159
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:33,980
Tiny! Butch, come out! This isn't funny!

160
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,860
I'm here to take you home!

161
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,737
Holy... Sh...

162
00:12:51,820 --> 00:12:53,180
Sh...

163
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:18,920
Good grief.

164
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:22,220
I have a soft spot for kid dog lovers.

165
00:13:22,660 --> 00:13:23,960
Lucky for him.

166
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,800
Tiny Pudge!

167
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:53,900
I didn't want to get involved,
but it's up to me now!

168
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:03,000
He had finally revealed his stand,

169
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:07,709
confirming Pet Shop's suspicions about
Iggy's extraordinary canine abilities.

170
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,294
Bring it, Feather Boy!

171
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:11,780
I can't wait to rip you to shreds!

172
00:14:13,340 --> 00:14:15,877
The Falcon is known
for its ability to dive

173
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,520
at speeds of over 300 kilometers per hour,

174
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:21,357
making it the fastest
animal on the planet.

175
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:26,480
Even at its trademark speed, the falcon
can spot its quarry with pinpoint accuracy.

176
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:31,800
The prey once discovered faces a violent
death by way of razor-sharp talons.

177
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:39,170
Huh?

178
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:40,380
What the?

179
00:14:40,620 --> 00:14:42,117
Did he just smirk at me?

180
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:45,840
I could have sworn I saw the
corners of its beak creep up,

181
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:49,000
but birds can't smile, can they?

182
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,300
Wait, what's going on here?

183
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,480
The air, it's getting colder.

184
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:02,657
Ice is coming out of the ground!

185
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:03,799
I'm such an idiot!

186
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:07,737
I was so focused on the bird, I didn't
realize my feet were frozen over.

187
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:09,460
My stance feet froze too!

188
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,030
Shit!

189
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,700
Icicles!

190
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,534
Come on, give it to me straight, Avdol.

191
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:51,597
Do you honestly believe that guy has
any chance of finding Dio's mansion?

192
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:54,357
I certainly hope so,
because if he can't find it,

193
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,457
there's no one left in this city who can.

194
00:15:56,540 --> 00:16:00,128
No one knows Cairo's complex
maze of streets better than him.

195
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,752
Try and have some faith.

196
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:04,197
Faith is something I'm
quickly running out of.

197
00:16:04,280 --> 00:16:07,997
We've been looking around this godforsaken
city for three days with no luck.

198
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:11,077
I highly doubt some beggar will
find the mansion in three hours.

199
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:14,077
You're starting to sound like
a broken record, Polnareff.

200
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:16,197
You could at least try
to keep a level head.

201
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:18,537
Listen up, we're all on edge right now.

202
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:22,397
Until our friend gets back, all we
can do is try talking to the locals.

203
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:23,420
Oh, brother.

204
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:26,937
And to make matters worse,
we haven't seen Iggy all day.

205
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:29,297
Where the hell did that
stupid mutt run off to?

206
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:30,840
He better not be lost.

207
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:34,317
For as long as I've known him, Iggy's
always been somewhat of a loner.

208
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:36,797
So I'm sure he's just
wandering around somewhere,

209
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:39,056
killing time before coming back home.

210
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:43,697
I used to think all dogs lit up and
wagged their tails when they saw humans.

211
00:16:43,780 --> 00:16:46,251
How'd we get stuck with that little cynic?

212
00:16:51,660 --> 00:16:53,900
I managed to get away from it somehow.

213
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:59,635
It's Stan's ice attack took
the skin right off my paws.

214
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,210
Damn it.

215
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:04,537
I knew I should have let that
human kid fix his own problems.

216
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:06,797
It's Stan's power is nothing to sneeze at.

217
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,400
That was no ordinary ice.

218
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:11,478
And I bet he still has a few tricks.

219
00:17:12,840 --> 00:17:15,781
I better get out of here
while the getting's good.

220
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,600
Talk about holding a grudge!

221
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,550
Ah!

222
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,600
Iggy disappeared.

223
00:18:00,160 --> 00:18:02,120
But where could he have gone?

224
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,520
Damn it!

225
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:11,590
That hurt.

226
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:13,757
The bastard doesn't hold anything back.

227
00:18:13,840 --> 00:18:14,880
He's strong.

228
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,700
For a dumb bird.

229
00:18:19,860 --> 00:18:21,817
This place reeks, but
it'll have to do for now.

230
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:25,724
We have to keep quiet in the
hideout down here until he gives up.

231
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:31,460
What is this freaky burnt steel?!

232
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:50,010
Hey!

233
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:54,710
Surprise!

234
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:56,997
Thought you had me, didn't you?

235
00:18:57,080 --> 00:19:00,492
But what you killed was my
shape-shifting stand, the fool!

236
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:05,610
Yeah!

237
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:08,549
How do you like them
apples, Feather Brain?

238
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,471
Might want to keep still.

239
00:19:16,800 --> 00:19:18,997
Looks like you're losing
a lot of blood there.

240
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:22,277
But before this drags out any
further, You should probably know.

241
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:25,595
I don't give a rat's ass
about you or your master deal.

242
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:27,898
What do you say we call this a draw?

243
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:32,514
You got a few good hits in with those
ice missiles, so we're even, right?

244
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:38,540
What the hell was that?

245
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:41,192
Who does this guy think he is, Bruce Lee?

246
00:19:41,600 --> 00:19:43,097
Hey, can't you hear?

247
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:45,677
I said I'll stay away
from your boss's mansion.

248
00:19:45,760 --> 00:19:47,180
Let's stop this, okay?

249
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:11,861
That's what your skin looks like?

250
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:13,860
What am I gonna do now? No!

251
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:22,257
You stopped your wound from
bleeding by freezing it?

252
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:24,000
What the hell? Ah!

253
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:25,390
Last it!

254
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:28,020
Oh no, the exit's blocked with ice!

255
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,900
Everyone's coming this way!

256
00:20:31,580 --> 00:20:32,410
Shit!

257
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,578
It's time to cover the whole tunnel!

258
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:39,491
I gotta find a way out of this death trap!

259
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:54,633
No way you plucked off this engine, too!

260
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:07,990
Crap.

261
00:21:08,073 --> 00:21:09,517
It's got me in its crosshairs.

262
00:21:09,600 --> 00:21:10,720
This bird's insane!

263
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:13,675
This is more than sheer determination.

264
00:21:13,780 --> 00:21:15,897
This creep's a frickin' killin' machine!

265
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:19,862
And if it catches me, it won't
just kill me, it'll leave me alive!

266
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:30,790
What?

267
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:33,760
No, it's my ball!

268
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:37,860
I can't prevent my pull-a-loose!

269
00:22:16,020 --> 00:22:17,640
Thank you.

270
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:53,400
Thank you.

271
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,809
Can my luck get any worse?

272
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,437
That lousy fleabag.

273
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:32,180
That bird is pissing me off!

274
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:34,377
It didn't occur to me until a moment ago,

275
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:36,957
but a stand user is likely
to be guarding Dio's lair.

276
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:41,393
Either way you slice it, I don't have
much choice, so it's do or die time!
